## SDD mode (merge into orchestrator)

Add to your orchestrator's classify table:

| **SDD** | "Start SDD", "Start SDD Lite", "Start SDD Review", "Continue SDD", "spec this feature", "speckit", "SDD", "sdd", "sdd-remote", "spec-driven", new multi-step feature when `.specify/` exists |

Add routing block:

**SDD** (Spec-Driven Development — see [docs/WORKFLOW-STAGES.md](../../docs/WORKFLOW-STAGES.md) and [docs/ADOPTION.md](../../docs/ADOPTION.md))
- Entry = `.cursor/skills/sdd-entry/SKILL.md` only (Start SDD / Continue SDD). Never invoke bare `speckit-*` as the top-level skill.
- Every phase goes through **`sdd-orchestrator`** + **`sdd-ctl`** (plan → worker → hooks → judge/swarm → record). Worker procedure = matching `speckit-*` skill. Workers never write `phase-exits.md`.
- Resolve `FEATURE_DIR` (`specs/NNN-*`, or `.specify/reviews/pr-<n>/` for Review) + next `PHASE`, then run the orchestrator for that phase (`auto_chain` from chat; `single_phase` from Spec Kit workflows).
- **Full** phase order: `specify → clarify → plan → tasks → analyze → implement → converge → confidence`. Analyze always runs; do not skip it.
- **Lite** phase order: `specify → plan → implement → light_gate`.
- **Review** phase order: `inspect → verdict`.
- Passing phases auto-continue. Failures repair up to the configured cap, then stop. Optional `"gate_mode": "interactive"` in `.specify/orchestrator.json` pauses after pass.
- Do not skip clarify before plan; do not implement without `tasks.md` on Full; do not start remote implement after a `tasks` pass — remote starts at `analyze`.
- Quality gates: `{LINT_CMD}` and `{TEST_CMD}` (also via `.specify/orchestrator.json` `implement_hooks` when `allow_repo_commands: true`).
- CLI: `specify workflow run sdd` (flags: `scope`, `stop_at`, `issues`, `mode`) or `sdd-remote`.
- On compact/checkpoint during SDD: include `tasks.md` progress (completed/total) in handoff.

Requires global `~/.cursor/skills/sdd-orchestrator/` (symlink) + clone of [sdd-orchestrator](https://github.com/Wade-O-Lution-Inc/sdd-orchestrator) at `~/.cursor/sdd-orchestrator-ctl/` — see [docs/ADOPTION.md](../../docs/ADOPTION.md) and the repository README.

